Task 3: State Modelling and Transition Verification
3.1 State definitions
A state describes what the robot is currently doing. An event is something that happens and may cause a change of state.
For example, NAVIGATING is a state, whereas ObstacleDetected is an event.
State ID	State	Meaning	Entry condition	Exit condition
ST-00	OFF	Robot is powered off.	Power is off.	Power-on signal.
ST-01	IDLE	Robot waits for a valid delivery request.	Startup completed or robot returned to warehouse.	Valid request or shutdown.
ST-02	NAVIGATING	Robot travels to its destination.	Valid delivery request accepted.	Obstacle, destination reached, critical battery, or safety fault.
ST-03	AVOIDING_OBSTACLE	Robot suspends normal navigation to handle an obstacle.	Obstacle detected during navigation.	Obstacle cleared and route verified, or safety fault.
ST-04	DELIVERING	Robot performs the delivery.	Destination reached and delivery conditions verified.	Delivery completed or a safety fault.
ST-05	RETURNING	Robot travels back to the warehouse.	Delivery completed, or delivery abandoned due to critical battery.	Warehouse reached or safety fault.
ST-06	SAFE_MODE	Robot performs its defined protective actions.	Critical battery/thermal condition or another defined critical fault.	Fault cleared and recovery checks passed.
ST-07	LINK_LOST	Remote communication is unavailable.	Communication timeout or link-loss detection.	Link restored and communication integrity verified.
Design assumption: SAFE_MODE and LINK_LOST are protective states that take precedence over normal activities. If both conditions occur, Safe Mode takes priority, while the link-loss condition remains recorded. The exact recovery policy must be approved by the safety authority.
3.2 Events and conditions
Event ID	Event	Meaning
EV-01	PowerOn	Robot receives a startup signal.
EV-02	DeliveryRequest	A delivery request is submitted.
EV-03	RequestValidated	Request and destination pass validation.
EV-04	ObstacleDetected	An obstacle is detected in the route.
EV-05	ObstacleCleared	The obstacle is cleared and the route is confirmed safe.
EV-06	DestinationReached	Robot reaches the assigned destination.
EV-07	DeliveryCompleted	Delivery is confirmed complete.
EV-08	WarehouseReached	Robot reaches the warehouse.
EV-09	CriticalBattery	Battery capacity falls below the emergency threshold.
EV-10	CriticalThermal	A chamber or battery temperature exceeds its critical threshold.
EV-11	LinkTimeout	The remote link is declared lost.
EV-12	LinkRestored	The remote link returns and is verified.
EV-13	FaultCleared	The critical fault is cleared and recovery checks pass.
EV-14	DoorOpened	The conservation chamber door opens.
EV-15	SensorFailure	An essential sensor fails.
3.3 State transition table
A valid transition is permitted by the specified model. An invalid transition must be rejected or prevented by the controller.
Transition ID	Current state + event	Next state	Req. ID	Valid?	Verification evidence
TR-01	OFF + PowerOn	IDLE	FR-01	Yes	TC-01
TR-02	IDLE + ValidatedDeliveryRequest	NAVIGATING	FR-02	Yes	TC-02
TR-03	IDLE + DeliveryRequest without validation	IDLE	FR-02	Yes, reject request	TC-02
TR-04	NAVIGATING + ObstacleDetected	AVOIDING_OBSTACLE	FR-04	Yes	TC-05
TR-05	AVOIDING_OBSTACLE + ObstacleCleared and route verified	NAVIGATING	FR-04	Yes	TC-05
TR-06	NAVIGATING + DestinationReached and delivery conditions verified	DELIVERING	FR-05	Yes	TC-06
TR-07	DELIVERING + DeliveryCompleted	RETURNING	FR-05	Yes	Delivery integration test
TR-08	RETURNING + WarehouseReached	IDLE	FR-01	Yes	Return-to-warehouse test
TR-09	NAVIGATING + CriticalBattery	RETURNING	FR-06	Yes, if return is safe	TC-07
TR-10	NAVIGATING + CriticalThermal or critical battery trigger	SAFE_MODE	SAFE-01	Yes	TC-08
TR-11	NAVIGATING + LinkTimeout	LINK_LOST	SAFE-03	Yes	TC-10
TR-12	LINK_LOST + LinkRestored and integrity verified	Previous safe operational state	SAFE-03	Conditional	Communication recovery test
TR-13	Any active state + critical safety trigger	SAFE_MODE	SAFE-01	Yes	TC-08
TR-14	AVOIDING_OBSTACLE + CriticalBattery	RETURNING or SAFE_MODE	FR-06 / SAFE-01	Conditional	Fault-injection test
